# The DISCRIMINATOR between the two readings alloc_churn_str.la left open.
#
# alloc_churn.la (ints only) grows without bound. alloc_churn_str.la (a string
# EVERY iteration) plateaus hard at 137 MB. Two explanations fit that equally:
#   (1) the blob path's own reclamation works where FREE24's does not, so the
#       24-byte cells leak regardless of what else is happening; or
#   (2) blob allocation merely DRIVES collection often (or thoroughly) enough
#       that the cells get swept too — i.e. the cells CAN be reclaimed, and the
#       int-only loop simply never triggers whatever does it.
#
# They predict opposite results for RARE blob allocation — one string every
# 1000 iterations:
#   under (1) the cells still leak -> RSS GROWS with N, like the int-only case;
#   under (2) the occasional string still drives collection -> RSS PLATEAUS.
# *** CORRECTED 2026-07-19. The first version wrote the loop as
#   SEQ(concat(...))(self(...))
# which puts the RECURSIVE CALL IN ARGUMENT POSITION. Arguments are evaluated on
# application, so that is NOT a tail call, TCO does not apply, the dump grows and
# the program dies with `native: stack overflow` (exit 134) at a FIXED depth.
# Its constant RSS was the memory in hand AT THE CRASH, and I read it as a
# steady-state plateau. It was not. The allocation is now the ARGUMENT and
# self(...) is the BODY, so the recursion is genuinely in tail position.
glyph Z    = la f. (la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))(la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))
glyph IF   = la c. la t. la f. c(t)(f)("!")
glyph SEQ  = la a. la b. b
glyph LOOP = Z(la self. la n.
    IF(int_eq(n)(0))(la _. "done")(la _.
      (la s. self(sub(n)(1)))
        (IF(int_eq(mod(n)(1000))(0))
           (la _. concat("abcdefgh")("ijklmnop"))
           (la _. "!"))))
glyph MAIN = print(LOOP(str_to_int(read_file("churn.n"))))
